---METADATA---
TARGET: packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx
DESCRIPTION: Main landing page that orchestrates the entire roast flow
DEPENDENCIES: 08-use-wallet-analysis.prompt, 09-use-roast-generator.prompt, 10-roast-card-component.prompt, 11-loading-roast-component.prompt, 12-share-buttons-component.prompt
PRIORITY: high
---END_METADATA---

Create the main page component that orchestrates the wallet roasting experience.

Requirements:
- Use "use client" directive (client component)
- Import useAccount from "wagmi"
- Import RainbowKitCustomConnectButton from "~~/components/scaffold-eth"
- Import custom hooks: useWalletAnalysis, useRoastGenerator
- Import components: RoastCard, LoadingRoast, ShareButtons

State machine:
1. INITIAL - Show landing page with connect button
2. CONNECTED - Show "Roast My Wallet" button
3. ANALYZING - Show loading while fetching transactions
4. GENERATING - Show loading while AI generates roast
5. DISPLAYING - Show RoastCard with results

Page Layout:

**Header Section:**
- Title: "🔥 ROAST MY WALLET 🔥"
- Subtitle: "Turn your cringe on-chain history into shareable entertainment"
- Connect button (if not connected)

**Initial State:**
- Hero section with example roast cards (optional for MVP)
- Big "Connect Wallet" button
- Brief explanation

**Connected State:**
- Show connected address
- Big "Roast My Wallet" button
- Loading indicator while analyzing

**Roast Display State:**
- RoastCard component with all data
- ShareButtons component below
- "Roast Again" button to regenerate

**Error Handling:**
- Show friendly error messages
- Provide retry button
- Handle cases:
  - No transactions found
  - API errors
  - Network errors

Styling:
- Full-screen layout with gradient background
- Center content vertically and horizontally
- Use Tailwind + daisyUI components
- Responsive design
- Dark theme
- Smooth transitions between states

Flow Logic:
1. User connects wallet → auto-fetch transactions
2. User clicks "Roast My Wallet" → generate roast
3. Display results with share options
4. "Roast Again" clears and restarts

Add proper TypeScript types.
Include loading states and error boundaries.
Make it fun and engaging!
